eason: It develops a minor piece to an active square, targets the exposed black king on e6, creates long-term pressure, and forces Black into a defensive posture early. Compared to pawn moves or rook shuffles, this is the most dynamic and threatening choice.\n\nAnswer: B: f8-c5"}
