 by Black? d8 is on the d-file. Who controls it? Black has no rook or queen on d-file. King was on d7, but after move, it leaves. So no — d8 is not under attack before or after. So rook can safely deliver check.\n\nThus, **R: e8-d8** is a free check, forcing the king to move, disrupting Black’s position, and likely winning material or leading to mate.\n\nReason: This move exploits the exposed position of the black king by delivering an immediate check with the rook, forcing the king into retreat and creating tactical opportunities. It is the most aggressive and effective use of tempo.\n\nAnswer: R: e8-d8"}
