hey don’t take, I have a rook on b8 with massive pressure — threatening Ra8+, Ka7, etc.\n\nAlso, note that Black has rooks on f7 and g7 — they might counterattack, but my position is solid.\n\nAnother idea: **B: d6-c7** — threatens to trap the king or prepare for a battery. But not as forcing.\n\n**R: d8-b8** is a capture, removes a piece near the king, and creates immediate threats.\n\nReason: The black king is abnormally positioned on b7 — likely due to early king movement — and the knight on b8 is its only close defender. Capturing it with Rxb8 forces either immediate material loss or severe weakening of Black’s position. It’s a high-pressure move that maximizes initiative.\n\nAnswer: R: d8-b8"}
