- R: b1-h1 – Activates the rook along the h-file toward the enemy king, possibly preparing for an attack.\n- K: h2-g1/h3 – King moves are passive and waste tempo when development is urgent.\n\nThe most promising move is **B: c5-e7**, which captures the undefended black pawn on e7. This gains material and opens lines near the black king. Since the black king is on b7, after Be7, it may be forced to move or lose more material. Additionally, capturing on e7 increases pressure and activity.\n\nReason: Capturing the pawn on e7 is a free material gain and increases pressure around the black king. It improves piece activity and avoids wasting tempo on passive development. No other move offers such a concrete advantage.\n\nAnswer: B: c5-e7"}
