k:\n- g1: safe\n- g3: captures pawn\n- h1: safe\n- h3: safe\n\nAmong these, **capturing the pawn on g3 is best** — it removes a threat, gains material, and centralizes the king slightly.\n\nReason: The black pawn on g3 is attacking my king on h2, placing me in check. I must respond by moving the king or capturing the pawn. Capturing the pawn with Kxg3 eliminates the immediate threat, improves my position, and prevents future dangers. Other king moves are passive and allow the pawn to remain as a latent threat.\n\nAnswer: K: h2-g3'}
