-h8? Yes, it\'s in the valid moves list: "R: f8-h8"\n\nThat seems strongest.\n\nReason: Rf8-h8 immediately targets the enemy rook on h1 by taking control of the h-file. With no pieces blocking, this creates a direct threat to win material. Black will likely have to waste a move responding, allowing me to consolidate or improve my other pieces. Compared to slow pawn pushes or king shuffles, this is the most active and forcing move.\n\nAnswer: R: f8-h8'}
