th limited material, rook activity is key. Placing the rook on d8 maximizes influence, potentially cutting off the black king or doubling with the pawn advance later. While king centralization is important, immediate rook activation offers greater dynamic potential and limits Black’s options.\n\nAnswer: R: a8-d8'}
