ential against the exposed black king on c6.\n\nReason: Promoting to a queen maximizes pressure and allows immediate threats of checkmate, especially combined with the rook or king support. While underpromotion (e.g., to knight) can sometimes create forks, in this position the queen provides the broadest range of winning possibilities, including direct checks and coordination with the rook or king.\n\nAnswer: P: a7-a8-q"}
