es (like Kg3-f4) are slow and lose time; the win should be forced with the queen.\n\nBest immediate action: Deliver check to reduce escape squares and drive the king toward the edge.\n\nQe8-g6+ forces the black king to move under duress and potentially walk into a mating net.\n\nReason: A check with the queen maximizes pressure and limits counterplay. Qe8-g6 is both a check and positions the queen to support a quick checkmate in coordination with the king if needed. It drives the black king toward the edge (h8 corner), where checkmate is easier to deliver.\n\nAnswer: Q: e8-g6"}
